==English==
[[File:Police issue X26 TASER-white.jpg|thumb|alt=Photograph of a Taser|Police-issue X26 '''Taser'''.]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈteɪz.ə(ɹ)/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|eɪzə(r)|lang=en}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[Taser]]

===Etymology===
{{acronym of|[[wikipedia:Tom Swift|Thomas A. Swift]]'s [[electric|Electric]] [[rifle|Rifle]]|lang=en}} Coined in the early 1970s by inventor Jack Cover, after the fictional character created by [[wikipedia:Edward Stratemeyer|Edward Stratemeyer]] in 1910 and especially the volume ''Tom Swift and His Electric Rifle'' (1911). Genericization of the trademark [[Taser]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈteɪz.ə(ɹ)/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|eɪzə(r)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|Taser}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[Taser]], a [[handheld]] [[device]] made by {{w|Taser International}} intended to [[immobilize]] another by delivering an [[electric]] [[shock]]; a [[stun gun]].
# By generalization, any electroshock stun gun.

